  "narrative": "No assessments are due and the voluntary independent-validation quota is exhausted, so this repaired explore step registers only valid discovery proposals. The prior validation failure came from putting cas9_activity_score in both eligibility and subgroup; these new comparisons avoid variable overlap by either using cas9_activity_score as an eligibility condition with no subgroup, or as a subgroup condition with no eligibility overlap. I retain the controller-signed convention: more negative dependency_composite means stronger dependency; for direction -1 direct claims, raw exposed-minus-comparator is expected negative if the exposed contrast has stronger dependency, and positive signed evidence means stronger dependency; for direction +1 direct claims, raw exposed-minus-comparator is expected positive if the exposed contrast has weaker dependency, and positive signed evidence supports weaker dependency or a positive interaction favoring the claim. For interactions, a positive signed estimate means the named subgroup has a larger raw effect in the claimed direction than the complement. The meaningfulness threshold is 0.15 absolute dependency-composite units, and invalid sparse cells are noninformative rather than evidence against a claim. The scientific need now is technical robustness and context refinement, not broad marker discovery. I registered high-observed-Cas9 main-effect tests for SMARCA4-loss, KEAP1-loss, TP53-loss, MSI-high, and PTEN-loss. These require cas9_activity_score >= 0.9, so they exclude lines missing observed editing activity and apply only to screens with Cas9 scores; they do not imply causal effects of Cas9 activity. For PTEN-loss, whose broad moderate stronger-dependency association is accepted but localization is heterogeneous, I added high-Cas9 lower-ploidy and elevated-aneuploidy contexts while excluding MSI-high and SMARCA4-loss backgrounds to reduce confounding by the strongest alternative markers. I also registered pairwise interaction tests among dominant markers: whether SMARCA4-loss effect modification occurs in KEAP1-loss or TP53-loss backgrounds, and whether KEAP1-loss or TP53-loss effects differ in SMARCA4-loss backgrounds. These are observational epistasis-like context tests; plausible alternatives to biological interaction include marker co-occurrence, compositional differences, ceiling/floor effects, correlated quality metrics, or batch structure. Finally, I registered a PTEN-loss interaction by high observed Cas9 activity, excluding MSI-high and SMARCA4-loss, to test whether PTEN-loss localization is partly technical. CDKN2A-loss is not newly promoted because recent less-overfitted context tests were mostly unsupported, below threshold, or imprecise; only an already valid clean narrow context could justify further CDKN2A work. All conclusions remain dataset-specific and observational, without causality, single-gene knockout interpretation, or clinical generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 repaired explore update. No assessments are due; voluntary validation remaining_new_requests=0. Controller-maintained accepted set unchanged. Core dataset-specific conclusions remain: SMARCA4-loss is the strongest robust stronger-dependency association; MSI-high is strong robust stronger-dependency; KEAP1-loss is strong discovery-supported weaker-dependency but not independently validated; TP53-loss is robust weaker-dependency; PTEN-loss is moderate stronger-dependency overall with heterogeneous localization; CDKN2A-loss is at most a narrow unresolved candidate, not a broad marker. Negative or unsupported tested predictors include ARID1A-loss, STK11-loss, KRAS mutation, PIK3CA mutation, BRAF V600E, BRCA2-loss, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, broad MYC amplification, broad sex, media serum 10 vs 5, Avana library, matched omics, constructed research markers/signatures, and most tested interactions. New registered hypotheses: high-observed-Cas9 main effects for SMARCA4-loss, KEAP1-loss, TP53-loss, MSI-high, and PTEN-loss; PTEN-loss high-Cas9 lower-ploidy and elevated-aneuploidy contexts excluding MSI-high and SMARCA4-loss; dominant-marker pairwise interactions among SMARCA4-loss, KEAP1-loss, and TP53-loss; and PTEN-loss effect modification by high Cas9 after excluding MSI-high and SMARCA4-loss. Interpretive rules: for direct direction -1 claims, positive signed means stronger dependency; for direct direction +1 claims, positive signed means weaker dependency or positive association in claimed direction. Cas9-conditioned analyses exclude missing cas9_activity_score and apply only to screens with observed editing scores. Interactions may reflect biological context, but also composition/co-occurrence, correlated technical quality, or batch effects. If high-Cas9 contexts give signed lower bounds above 0.15, they support robustness; if near threshold, imprecise, null, or invalid, they do not promote the claim. If scheduled validation appears later, highest-priority validation targets remain broad high-quality KEAP1-loss, PTEN-loss localization, and only a genuinely valid clean narrow CDKN2A context."
